WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
The one piece manga just showed the secret ruler&nbsp;
of the world government speaking for the very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.020
first time. And with just a single word, we learn&nbsp;
that the ancient war between the world government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:15.960
and the Ancient Kingdom might actually have been&nbsp;
an insane love triangle drama that changed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.120
entire world. At the center of all this is this&nbsp;
brand new character who was queen of Alabasta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.760
at the end of the void century, and in this&nbsp;
chapter we get hints about her crazy ties to Imu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.880
Joy Boy, and even Amazon Lily. And you’re&nbsp;
not ready for the incredible theory about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.780
characters from the void century that&nbsp;
we’ll discuss at the end of the video.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:43.080
Starting with the former Queen of Alabasta,&nbsp;
Lily. Just like with the holy knights last week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.100
we are introduced to this character for the&nbsp;
very first time in this chapter, when Cobra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:53.640
the king of Alabasta – at least, before he was&nbsp;
assassinated – asks the Five Elders about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:58.200
past. He comments that the 20 swords jammed&nbsp;
into the ground before Imu’s throne belonged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.360
to the original 20 kingdoms that founded the world&nbsp;
government. He then asks about Lily. Apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.160
she was queen at the end of the Void century,&nbsp;
making this only the fourth named character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.920
who is absolutely confirmed to be from this&nbsp;
time period along with Joy Boy and Zunesha,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:19.440
and one other we will discuss later on.&nbsp;
However, after the war, she disappeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:25.920
and was never seen again. Cobra mentions that&nbsp;
of the 20 swords, only 19 actually remain. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.580
he then even goes on to confront the Gorosei about&nbsp;
the will of D, about which the royal family has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.740
passed down information through the centuries&nbsp;
and which seems to be connected to Lily and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:44.580
the founding of the world government. Now where&nbsp;
did Lily go? Let’s see if we can figure it out.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.940
First, you might remember that&nbsp;
at the end of the void century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.620
the twenty kingdoms defeated the Ancient Kingdom&nbsp;
and then formed the World Government. We first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.200
learned in chapter 722 that the other nineteen&nbsp;
rulers went up to Mary Geoise and became the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:04.020
Celestial Dragons, but Lily refused&nbsp;
to join them in the holy land. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.100
why did she do this? Well, there are a few&nbsp;
reasons that we are going to speculate.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.900
The most likely reason is that somehow the&nbsp;
country of Alabasta was actually friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:19.080
with the Ancient Kingdom. We know this because&nbsp;
in chapter 202 it is confirmed that Alabasta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.840
has been keeping a Poneglyph hidden from the&nbsp;
world government ever since the Void Century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:32.700
And now not just any kingdom can have these&nbsp;
stones. And that is because the poneglyphs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.500
record the history of the Void Century and&nbsp;
other information that the Ancient Kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.300
did not want the World Government to erase.&nbsp;
And we see all throughout the story that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.020
poneglyphs were given to the allies of&nbsp;
the ancient kingdom all throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.360
world. These include Fishman Island, Zou,&nbsp;
Shandora, Wano, and apparently Alabasta.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.960
And even though they have had&nbsp;
the poneglyph for over 800 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.580
Cobra still fiercely protected the&nbsp;
secret, even willing to sacrifice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:05.460
his own life to stop Crocodile from finding&nbsp;
it. So clearly it was important and probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:11.880
not just something they randomly found.&nbsp;
So how does this connect back to Lily?

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.200
Well, if Alabasta and Lily were friends with the&nbsp;
ancient Kingdom, then we have to ask how they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.820
ended up being one of the twenty kingdoms&nbsp;
that defeated the ancient kingdom. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:26.580
while we don’t know for sure, it is possible that&nbsp;
someone from Alabasta, maybe even Lily herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.860
betrayed the ancient kingdom, which helped the&nbsp;
twenty kingdoms to win the war. Maybe they killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.660
Joy Boy or somehow gave the twenty kingdoms&nbsp;
secret information. But whatever the reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.500
it seems like the outcome caused&nbsp;
Lily to reject the other kingdoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:45.180
and even her own kingdom,&nbsp;
to disappear into the world.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.140
So with this in mind, let’s take a closer&nbsp;
look at who Lily actually could be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:54.480
what she might have done, and also the tangled&nbsp;
web of her relationships from the void century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.760
So get your popcorn ready everyone, because we’re&nbsp;
about to dive headfirst into a juicy love affair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:05.340
Starting with Lily and Joy Boy, who could very&nbsp;
easily have been in love with each other. Let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:10.140
me explain. For the longest time in the story, we&nbsp;
knew that Joy Boy and Zunesha were from the Void&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:15.720
Century. And now that we know Lily was as well,&nbsp;
it makes sense that she would be connected to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:21.120
other two. Now that could mean the Alabasta was&nbsp;
friends with the ancient kingdom and Lily and Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:27.600
Boy became friends this way. Or maybe Lily was&nbsp;
a pirate, since the ancient kingdom was likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.880
a kingdom of pirates, and then she only became&nbsp;
queen of Alabasta for a short time after the war.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:37.320
But however they met, we know she gave&nbsp;
everything up for some reason after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:42.060
war. And what is the only thing that we know&nbsp;
for sure about the war. That the Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:46.680
Kingdom lost and Joy Boy couldn’t fulfill&nbsp;
his plans. *looks around nervously. Wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:52.440
we do know this right?? Oda isn’t going to&nbsp;
trick us with this either, is he?? But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.540
makes a lot of sense to me that she was either&nbsp;
heartbroken that Joy Boy had died during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.940
war or that she was so ashamed of betraying him&nbsp;
that she decided to abandon her life as queen.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:08.280
But then where did she go? Well, there is&nbsp;
one obvious place that would fit perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:14.340
with what we’ve explained so far. The&nbsp;
island of women, Amazon Lily. Now clearly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:19.380
both the character and the island share the name&nbsp;
Lily, and even in Japanese this word is written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:25.140
the exact same way. Which by the way, did you&nbsp;
also know that in Japanese culture the lily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:31.320
flower can represent purity, revenge, or even&nbsp;
a final goodbye for the dead, all depending on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:38.040
