00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:45.720
And to take this idea a little further, if&nbsp;
Imu and Lily were in love, what if they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:52.320
a child and that child became the ruler of&nbsp;
Alabasta. So, I know it sounds crazy, but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:58.260
is possible that Vivi could be a descendant of&nbsp;
Imu and that is why Imu was holding her picture.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.160
Plus, Lily and Vivi look shockingly similar,&nbsp;
so that’s one part this puzzle confirmed.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:13.920
But if imu and Lily were lovers, then we have to&nbsp;
ask why would Lily leave after the war. Certainly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:19.440
Imu is still alive so if their relationship is&nbsp;
actually true, couldn’t they just have snuggled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.400
up in that big castle. Well, something&nbsp;
would need to have changed during the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:27.360
of the war. Maybe – and this is where the&nbsp;
love triangle comes in – Lily was in love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:35.400
with both Joy Boy and Imu, and when Imu the&nbsp;
twenty kingdoms defeated the ancient kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:39.240
Lily was still so torn up about Joy&nbsp;
Boy’s defeat that she left anyway.

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:43.560
Or even if she was just in love with Imu,&nbsp;
maybe she was so disgusted by something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:47.580
Imu did during the war that she didn’t&nbsp;
want anything to do with them ever again.

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:53.040
But that’s a lot of speculation about a&nbsp;
lover’s feud, so let’s reign things in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.140
bit and get to another possibility about Lily.&nbsp;
And this time, the former queen of Alabasta&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.140 --> 00:12:02.040
is putting on that big pointy hat herself&nbsp;
[show Imu’s big hat/crown]. That’s right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:08.280
let’s discuss what could happen if Lily actually&nbsp;
became Imu. And let’s start by digging back into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:13.080
Japanese culture. Because the water Lilies&nbsp;
are also an important symbol in Buddhism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:18.180
